#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc0cb83-5eb1-5dd9-af9f-ee8ca5368146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260669} {:answer/id #uuid "788bb643-f360-5e75-ad92-1f1daf3b6599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260931} {:answer/id #uuid "c59fb9ed-aa8c-55a3-8bca-ec58a0283bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261618} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} {:answer/id #uuid "fede5c03-7967-5771-bc19-dd1e5e5a6385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a92faf-5d71-5f25-92c3-12fac1bc6f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f9b021c-bf51-5fc5-8b75-b8c974a0fbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128433" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a3758c-f60c-5dae-92fa-afedc78160ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458653} {:answer/id #uuid "1c111100-d619-5b93-b482-b6ec810b8df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458679} {:answer/id #uuid "3f06b20c-1420-5939-96cc-465d37b4df29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458746} {:answer/id #uuid "856f42a7-be02-543a-b498-4b18fecdaca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458860} {:answer/id #uuid "96678253-6e22-571e-98ff-a64d81bbbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96678253-6e22-571e-98ff-a64d81bbbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458889} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef466f3-b445-5f7c-961a-8d3a58c07b04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2eedb023-f05d-5365-a7fb-580375aea9cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-128442" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $p=⟨5,-2,2⟩,$ $q=⟨3,k,1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-8,3,-4⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k & 1 \\\\ -8 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(k\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot (-4)-(-8)\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 3-(-8)\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-20k-15-8+18+16k \\\\  & =-4k-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -4k-5 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{5}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6523e66f-3eae-532d-af4f-39b785b57f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378568} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0d16a7-95d1-5a5f-aa7e-734db7ae523b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378569} {:answer/id #uuid "9365d6aa-7405-5556-acfb-cdae2d97fb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378570} {:answer/id #uuid "03bf534f-e82e-5f46-aa2b-26e765dc8c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378571} {:answer/id #uuid "b288711d-0efe-5c03-b8d4-fcbdbce46686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03bf534f-e82e-5f46-aa2b-26e765dc8c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378571} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee88383b-1dff-5bb7-9ff0-c76d09dd0d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df2041e4-731a-5917-8788-670168bfca15" :question/math-academy-id "q-128453" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨8,4,6⟩,$ $b=⟨8,-4,5⟩,$ and $c=⟨0,2,k⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}|+6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8(-4\\cdot k-2\\cdot 5)-4(8\\cdot k-0\\cdot 5)+6(8\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-32k-80-32k+96 \\\\  & =16-64k \\\\  & =16(1-4k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 16(1-4k) & =0 \\\\ 1-4k & =0 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{1}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad8221b0-abe5-5ff1-bc3c-90d12161ae4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102151} {:answer/id #uuid "af030614-b019-5cb7-af82-49461aee453a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102152} {:answer/id #uuid "f7689ce5-7f20-51b0-9bf1-02cf4cfa28a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102153} {:answer/id #uuid "20089b8e-9e90-54c9-b1aa-d58c28a522ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102154} {:answer/id #uuid "415bcf68-6460-529e-98b7-2570d358ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415bcf68-6460-529e-98b7-2570d358ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102155} :answer-field/id #uuid "e745e616-1f75-5e2e-88b5-a1da5a69b25d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "292a1bfa-7936-5037-9015-22a88ecb52f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-128472" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(9,6,1),$ $B(9,7,2),$ $C(7,5,2),$ and $D(7,8,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(9i+7j+2k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(7i+5j+2k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =-2i-j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(7i+8j+3k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 1)+((-2)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =2-6 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-4|=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a42f150-af09-50f1-93e5-5a7ef6c3941c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378575} {:answer/id #uuid "0e61ab76-8c5d-5910-8b87-4c64f34d8f37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378576} {:answer/id #uuid "132eab41-9a12-5b05-a76e-570681089bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378577} {:answer/id #uuid "eeaa0c77-6439-57a3-810c-a0949283ed9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378578} {:answer/id #uuid "9c500f0c-3011-5638-86d3-c14893131d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c500f0c-3011-5638-86d3-c14893131d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378579} :answer-field/id #uuid "88508ed0-7bb9-51fe-90d6-2bd0fcd3f98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57ae3b89-c4ab-5dbf-a8d7-b1b9339d2673" :question/math-academy-id "q-128482" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,1),$ $B(0,-1,3),$ $C(1,-2,2),$ and $D(2,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-j+3k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-3i-j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-2j+2k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2j+k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-i+2j \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-2)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 1)+((-2)\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1)+2((-2)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =6+1-12 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-5|=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91deb4db-6b2a-544a-ba74-25f888d469ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102447} {:answer/id #uuid "c29df26f-2f8c-5d14-9196-e5107c54f911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102448} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8b0a72-6c5b-5545-80b7-68d22aa15109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102449} {:answer/id #uuid "d2285774-835c-5d92-9c39-8d811ec66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102450} {:answer/id #uuid "0a269770-4d2f-5b51-8afe-9049f4a722d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2285774-835c-5d92-9c39-8d811ec66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102450} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b8f48f-b324-5fdc-82a9-632d1ad15e21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b990ba56-2404-5f20-a869-596a97b7f65e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18268" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨3,t,t⟩$, $q=⟨1,3,1⟩$, and $r=⟨1,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & t & t \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)-t(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)+t(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =24-2t-2t \\\\  & =24-4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 24-4t & =0 \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4b54cc7-eae3-5d57-91d2-3a0fea3a1c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458919} {:answer/id #uuid "b303e1bb-f85e-5fac-8e2e-0800f3853ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "161" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458950} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8935c4-627d-5119-a734-99dcd8c66458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458972} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b30beb-61fb-5067-98b9-8e9d6b43d7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-134" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459017} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7b07bc-b3d2-5466-b600-1f239c376357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{155}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf8935c4-627d-5119-a734-99dcd8c66458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a5041e-ac12-543b-a288-c49e2bf1590e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "da5d7cb9-5c27-5b41-96e4-8767d3252a54" :question/math-academy-id "q-20144" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-2,2)$, $B(4,3,2)$, $C(1,3,5)$, $D(2,4,-6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+2k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+3j+5k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+5j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,5,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+4j-6k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+6j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-1,6,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-8)-6\\cdot 3)-5((-2)\\cdot (-8)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+0 \\\\  & =-58-95 \\\\  & =-153.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-153|=153.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17336941-881c-5fb2-a109-5b4a5addcfec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17336941-881c-5fb2-a109-5b4a5addcfec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483606} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6a81b1b-3ad2-556f-aea1-11eab91bed3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8951c125-ece2-55e4-a6b5-7a7f9b036e1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280669" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨3,0,-2⟩$, $y=⟨1,2,4⟩$, and $z=⟨-5,1,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1)+0+(-2)(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-5)) \\\\  & =-6-22 \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-28|=28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef21b691-d97c-5047-bd55-f0d2f57c360d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef21b691-d97c-5047-bd55-f0d2f57c360d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484042} :answer-field/id #uuid "752c7d24-ba0b-5853-99e8-14fd968c0d02" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54f335de-9889-5585-819e-c5ae71a53628" :question/math-academy-id "q-280714" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $p=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $q=⟨0,5,1⟩$, and $r=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0\\cdot 6-1\\cdot 4)+3(0\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =30+8-60 \\\\  & =-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-22|=22.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0618fdf5-9970-590e-8185-d4fd25d3af95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0618fdf5-9970-590e-8185-d4fd25d3af95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292957} :answer-field/id #uuid "03def6c9-038a-52fb-8620-4828ee17ec9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02a24008-f4b2-51f6-bfa2-34173306dcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-280720" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eea5ea1b-1584-5bf8-9c56-60e082cc3b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eea5ea1b-1584-5bf8-9c56-60e082cc3b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484039} :answer-field/id #uuid "aefbe563-901b-5005-9895-d7c05a2acfbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65ad1da6-49b7-5494-8267-2eea67ec5389" :question/math-academy-id "q-280747" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨2,k,-1⟩$, $b=⟨-3,4,5⟩$, and $c=⟨6,k,1⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 1-5\\cdot k)-k(-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)-1(-3\\cdot k-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =8-10k+33k+3k+24 \\\\  & =26k+32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 26k+32 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{16}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{16}{13}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "842559ea-e8de-579e-b0e2-e4bc6fd93411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104003} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b8cf03-23cd-55b9-a44e-0a91507aef2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104004} {:answer/id #uuid "07566dee-dcab-5b2b-aeff-bb244caaef53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104005} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf80ba1-1722-5eda-8a01-2202aeb56d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104006} {:answer/id #uuid "78cee756-b381-5b9c-8874-9a1d39a5f075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07566dee-dcab-5b2b-aeff-bb244caaef53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104005} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2fd0b9-0fb1-5157-8647-5b6a0eebb344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51de3e44-6cdb-5f9b-ba39-3a79c7ef7ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-40214" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨3,5,0⟩$, $y=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $z=⟨3,4,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 5-4\\cdot 0)-5(3\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 0)+0 \\\\  & =30-75 \\\\  & =-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|-45|=45.\n$$"}] 