by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-4)\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2)-2(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)+5(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =14-2+25 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|37|=37.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22269750-3610-50c1-9f1a-e32029db2cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339419} {:answer/id #uuid "82067827-a66f-5c6a-aae6-789419de79b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340299} {:answer/id #uuid "826586c2-1bf6-5265-9275-8aca9ef0a3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340301} {:answer/id #uuid "df70070c-22ea-53f2-a484-ebf2fd57d953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341114} {:answer/id #uuid "fc03c5f9-9d3d-5c25-b729-1dac1a0eaf64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82067827-a66f-5c6a-aae6-789419de79b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340299} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d6930c-5eff-59bb-a41f-2cb0e35d6542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1acfcbc-5797-5d52-8f43-51fb0ff9335f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73744" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,1,0)$, $B(-2,1,0)$, $C(3,2,0)$, and $D(1,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =-3i \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+1j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+3k)-(i+j) \\\\  & =3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)-0+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041ecafc-32e3-55b2-bd4d-16b2bb0a3485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339154} {:answer/id #uuid "12b4a91a-647d-55f9-aa8c-e6d3645734f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339293} {:answer/id #uuid "7833b55c-3b8d-5820-a478-1c02f596ba57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340200} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ef1d18-3b2d-548c-8803-d8c7d794cda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341193} {:answer/id #uuid "ed939920-d631-5c81-9821-0b25e67f578f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9ef1d18-3b2d-548c-8803-d8c7d794cda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341193} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f32398d-38d4-52b0-b5d4-56a201268afd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b26b4535-e272-5e94-b038-84726ee96584" :question/math-academy-id "q-73748" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,-1,0)$, $B(-1,2,-1)$, $C(1,1,2)$, and $D(3,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j-k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =i+k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-6+9+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|\\,5\\,|=5.\n$$"}]}
